## Configuration Files and Environment Variables

Application settings are declared in `core/src/main/resources/application.yml`. Placeholders like `${NAME:default}` allow easy overriding through environment variables or `.env` files. Docker Compose provides PostgreSQL, SMTP, public URL, Google settings, and maintenance mode defaults.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> OAuth secrets and sensitive credentials belong in the untracked `.env` file, never committed to version control.

### Primary Variables

| Variable | Purpose | Typical local value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED` | Enables the Google sign-in button | `false` until configured |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | OAuth Web application client ID | From Google Cloud Console |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | OAuth client secret | From Google Cloud Console |
| `WEB_BASE_URL` | Public HTTPS URL for redirects and email links | `https://localhost` |
| `MAINTENANCE_MODE` | Activates the maintenance landing page | `false` |
